msgid "/* All functionality for only admins */"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-02-types-implemented.md:43
msgid ""
"Here we're using a type parameter and gating permissions behind \"tag\" "
"types that implement different permission traits."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-02-types-implemented.md:46
msgid ""
"Tag types, or marker types, are zero-sized types that have some semantic "
"meaning to users and API designers."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-02-types-implemented.md:49
msgid ""
"Ask: What issues does having it be an actual instance of that type pose?"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-02-types-implemented.md:51
msgid ""
"Answer: If it's not a zero-sized type (like `()` or `struct MyTag;`), then "
"we're allocating more memory than we need to when all we care for is type "
"information that is only relevant at compile-time."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-02-types-implemented.md:55
msgid "Demonstrate: remove the `tag` value entirely, then compile!"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-02-types-implemented.md:57
msgid "This won't compile, as there's an unused (phantom) type parameter."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-02-types-implemented.md:59
msgid "This is where `PhantomData` comes in!"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-02-types-implemented.md:61
msgid ""
"Demonstrate: Uncomment the `PhantomData` import, and make `ChatId<T>` the "
"following:"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-02-types-implemented.md:74
msgid ""
"`PhantomData<T>` is a zero-sized type with a type parameter. We can "
"construct values of it like other ZSTs with `let phantom: "
"PhantomData<UserTag> = PhantomData;` or with the `PhantomData::default()` "
"implementation."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-02-types-implemented.md:79
msgid ""
"Demonstrate: implement `From<u64>` for `ChatId<T>`, emphasizing the "
"construction of `PhantomData`"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-02-types-implemented.md:90
msgid "// Or `PhantomData::default()`\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/borrow-checker-invariants/phantomdata-02-types-implemented.md:97
msgid ""
"`PhantomData` can be used as part of the Typestate pattern to have data with "
"the same structure but different methods, e.g., have `TaggedData<Start>` "
"implement methods or trait implementations that `TaggedData<End>` doesn't."
msgstr ""
